#: ../../source/docs/auto-mode.rst:5
#: f7c085d92b354dbbad8a58ce2a32fbab
msgid "AUTO Mode"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/auto-mode.rst:7
#: da7fb40431f34aef82992e07fea6d359
msgid "In AUTO mode Plane will follow a mission (a set of GPS waypoints and other commands) set by your ground station. When re-entering AUTO mode Plane will continue from whatever mission item it was last doing, unless you have reset the mission. If the mission ends with an item that does not continue indefinitely (like LOITER UNLIMITED), an RTL will be executed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/auto-mode.rst:12
#: b407a939166c4cdeb54efda61db6c346
msgid "When in AUTO Plane will by default allow the pilot to influence the flight of the plane by using \"stick mixing\", which allows for aileron, elevator and rudder input to steer the plane in a way that can override the autopilot control. Whether this is enabled is determined by the :ref:`STICK_MIXING <STICK_MIXING>` option. By default stick mixing behaves the same as :ref:`FLY BY WIRE_A (FBWA) <fbwa-mode>` mode."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/auto-mode.rst:19
#: 61990f531ac54bf19b697940c8f96af5
msgid "The speed during the mission is nominally at :ref:`AIRSPEED_CRUISE<AIRSPEED_CRUISE>` when using an airspeed sensor, or at whatever speed results from :ref:`TRIM_THROTTLE<TRIM_THROTTLE>` without an airspeed sensor. Setting :ref:`THROTTLE_NUDGE<THROTTLE_NUDGE>` = 1 allows the speed to be increased if the throttle stick is above mid-stick up to :ref:`AIRSPEED_MAX<AIRSPEED_MAX>` or :ref:`THR_MAX<THR_MAX>`, when using or not using an airspeed sensor, respectively."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/auto-mode.rst:23
#: a679390cf5b9444c8db6239b625a93c0
msgid "\"Home\" position is always supposed to be your Plane's actual GPS takeoff location:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/auto-mode.rst:26
#: 1916f24c33184388a1107dd8b2381cea
msgid "It is very important to acquire GPS lock before arming in order for RTL, Loiter, Auto or any GPS dependent mode to work properly."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/auto-mode.rst:28
#: fd46c81fd35642c0a5b0c14c12652233
msgid "For Plane the home position is initially established at the time the plane acquires its GPS lock. It is then continuously updated as long as the autopilot is disarmed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/auto-mode.rst:32
#: b29dbf97efdf41d1ad2522b2146c29c7
msgid "This means if you execute an RTL in Plane, it will return to the location where it was when it was armed - assuming it had acquired GPS lock."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/auto-mode.rst:33
#: a2c27a7bc0744bc0ad3b7b1cc7c7546a
msgid "Consider the use of :ref:`Rally Points <common-rally-points>` to avoid returning directly to your arming point on RTL."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/auto-mode.rst:36
#: b3195d67013245168ad47b475b2d0c89
msgid "MISSION INTERRUPTION"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/auto-mode.rst:38
#: cb8fdd55ff694ec28f7673fc275fc83e
msgid "Changing out of AUTO Mode leaves whatever mission item being executed in a \"suspended\" state. Re-entry into AUTO mode later will either resume execution of the mission where it was left or restart the mission depending on the value of the :ref:`MIS_RESTART<MIS_RESTART>` parameter. By default, it will resume. If you were on the way to Waypoint 3 when changed modes out of AUTO, if re-entered, it will immediately head for Waypoint 3 and continue the mission."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/auto-mode.rst:40
#: 175f80902d59428d8a6668ad05ae423e
msgid "You can reset the mission back to the beginning using either the ``RCx_OPTION`` switch \"24\", or via a MAVLink command. Mission Planner has a button in its \"Actions\" tab of the DATA screen to \"Restart Mission\". If :ref:`MIS_RESTART<MIS_RESTART>` is set to \"1\", the the mission will be reset to the start every time AUTO mode is entered."
msgstr ""
